--TEST--
two `extend` blocks in one program may not add one name to one type: the second block's member is `E1011`, and the error shows where the first block adds the name — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace App;

use Core\Time\Date;

extend Date as BusinessDays {
    public function isWeekend(): bool {
        return $this->day() == 6;
    }
}

extend Date as Weekdays {
    public function isWeekend(): bool {
        return $this->day() == 7;
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E1011]: the `extend` block `App\BusinessDays` already adds a method named `isWeekend`
   --> %s:7:21
   |
 7 |     public function isWeekend(): bool {
   |                     --------- `App\BusinessDays` adds `isWeekend` here
...
13 |     public function isWeekend(): bool {
   |                     ^^^^^^^^^ this name is already used
   = help: give the added member a different name. An added member never replaces or overrides another member

error: aborting due to 1 error
%A
